  "details": "It'd be really helpful to have a beta or launch option to use Oculus SDK instead of SteamVR on Steam.\nSteamVR runs like a hot mess, especially when loading into places.\nOculusClient is a mess that refuses to install things properly, and this means it'd be easier to keep up to date and be able to see people in the same room as me. This makes the Oculus version unusable. It doesn't even finish installing.\nOpenComposite currently doesn't work with VrChat on Steam by the way, so I'm stuck between a rock and a hard place.\nEither I run the game on Oculus, and I can't connect with anyone, or I run it on Steam and leg to death every time I load into a map, or an avatar gets loaded.\nThe other day my friend could see me but not hear me, while I couldn't see them or hear them at all, only their name.",
